The issue is that the current implementation of the `recite` function is generating "1 bottles of beer" instead of "1 bottle of beer". We need to fix the pluralization for the last bottle.

Here is the updated `beer_song.py` file with the fix:

beer_song.py
```
def recite(start, take=1):
    verses = []
    for i in range(start, start - take, -1):
        if i > 1:
            verses.append(f"{i} bottles of beer on the wall, {i} bottles of beer.")
            verses.append(f"Take one down and pass it around, {i-1} bottles of beer on the wall.")
        elif i == 1:
            verses.append(f"{i} bottle of beer on the wall, {i} bottle of beer.")
            verses.append(f"Take it down and pass it around, no more bottles of beer on the wall.")
        else:
            verses.append("No more bottles of beer on the wall, no more bottles of beer.")
            verses.append("Go to the store and buy some more, 99 bottles of beer on the wall.")
        if i != start - take + 1:
            verses.append("")  # Add a blank line between verses
    return verses
```

This should resolve the errors in the tests.
